      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jasper%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Jasper City post office opened in 1876, a milestone that some locals mark as the town’s true founding year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://jaspermo.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1881 the Missouri‑Pacific Railroad began developing and subdividing Jasper, laying the groundwork for the modern town layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
